spec: S09-08, S09-11

`push` renders at the edge and uploads the HTML with the commit; `rerender DOC` re-renders every
Version with the server's renderer and reports `name id versions changed` — the server's crate is
the CLI's crate, so a freshly pushed Document changes nothing. `--json` narrows like everywhere.
Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan push rr-plan.md -m "first"
assets: 1 referenced, 1 new (178 B)
rr-plan	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan rerender rr-plan
rerender: 1 Version, 0 changed (renderer [..])
rr-plan	[..]	1	0

$ annotary -p agent rerender rr-plan.md -q
rr-plan	[..]	1	0

$ annotary -p rowan push rr-plan.md -m "second" --json version,already
assets: 1 referenced, 0 new
{"version":1,"already":true}

$ annotary -p rowan rerender rr-plan --json
rerender: 1 Version, 0 changed (renderer [..])
{"name":"rr-plan","id":"[..]","versions":1,"changed":0}

$ annotary -p rowan rerender rr-plan -q --json versions,changed
{"versions":1,"changed":0}

```
